  "requiredChecks": [
    "checked-types",
    "checked-focused",
    "checked-legacy",
    "final-quality",
    "final-format",
    "final-registry",
    "final-inventory",
    "final-inventory-controls"
  ],
  "detail": "A live range owns canonical request/page syntax once per call. Its private verifier may borrow only this internally created lifetime; exported live APIs accept no parsed permission and cannot select stored mode. Bound legacy/page encoders accept event fields, never a supplied parsed object. Exact captured raw and decoded frame bytes are checked against private snapshots; structural metadata is frozen, the lifetime cannot cross structured clone, and cancellation/error/dispose erases owned raw/decoded/snapshot buffers while leaving callers and detached output bytes intact. All existing codec field/proof/extent/canonical checks and every entry crypto/chain/actor/scope/expiry/size/lifetime check remain. Existing default and stored paths stay independent. No native dense writer is enabled yet.",
  "validation": "Eight initial controls: seven fail and one passes before; the real eight-entry live path decodes each original17times before versus once after, retaining18signature checks. Added ninth final-crypto mutation control has no matched-before credit. Nine pass, including exact default codec agreement, interior dense syntax, metadata/clone, foreign originals, raw/decoded mutation, output/caller erasure and unchanged live expiry. Types,251focused cases across28files and18unchanged legacy pass; quality, format,17registry checks, inventory and10controls pass. Independent normalized AST review preserves all prior codec/verifier operations. Two runtime hashes/three source-site line moves reviewed, constructions/obligations/old tests unchanged. Latest full checkpoint remains412:323files/3161cases/one skip124.19s at240s; no redundant full rerun for this isolated slice.",
  "summary": "A live range and bound codecs now share one exact captured syntax lifetime;17decodes become1 with all18signature checks. Nine controls,251focused/18legacy cases and repository checks pass.",
  "limitations": "No native dense writer, physical cold, image, activation, latency or RAM credit. Snapshot copies deliberately preserve exact mutation checks; no RAM saving is claimed. Dense native writing, dual audit, G8/B, floor lifecycle, old artifacts/cold/rollback and Stage5/6 remain. No format/trust/wire/default/limit/gate/deadline change, commit or deployment.",
  "decisionTitle": "Bind live encoders to their own canonical originals",
  "decision": "Do not accept externally supplied parsed objects at an encoder or live verification boundary. A call-local lifetime owns syntax and bound encoders, retains exact current raw/frame checks and erasure, and shares no authority or permission across an owner or Worker. Existing per-entry crypto and canonical structural checks remain.",
  "next": "Implement bounded native dense preparation and its atomic physical receipt writing, then dual physical/logical audit, G8/B and floor/lifecycle/old artifacts/cold/rollback. Continue after each freeze under the latest automatic continuation instruction.",
  "progressEdits": [
    [
      "publication or deployment. Stop/report under the operator's functional/negative-\ncontrol/guard rules. New-code unit failures are ordinary development and retained.",
      "publication or deployment. Latest operator direction: continue after every phase;\nstop only for format/trust/limit/deadline decisions or failures unfixable within\nexisting guards. All failed attempts remain evidence."
    ],
    [
      "logical/actual-owned index and dual audit bounds. Census and saved verification\nstill capture separately: final per-load owned-page integration remains. Ordinary builds remain writer-off;",
      "logical/actual-owned index and dual audit bounds. Full/native/reduced loads and\nnew-row continuations now own their call-local syntax; live range parsing is owned\nas well. Ordinary builds remain writer-off;"
    ]
  ],
